==In animation==
===''Pokémon the Series''===
[[File:Team Magma Grunts anime.png|thumb|250px|Team Magma Grunts in {{aniseries|RS}}]]
Team Magma Grunts have made several appearances in ''Pokémon the Series: Ruby and Sapphire'', using their Pokémon to infiltrate a target or to help [[Tabitha]] out. Magma Grunts debuted in ''[[AG002|A Ruin with a View]]'', where they tried to find ancient Pokémon in the ruins under [[Oldale Town]]. They used [[Professor Alden]] to guide them there, and after collecting data from the ruins, escaped in their helicopter. In ''[[AG027|A Three Team Scheme!]]'', they dug into a special shrine underground on [[Dewford Town|Dewford Island]], searching for Groudon and the [[Cave of Origin]].

In ''[[AG036|The Spheal of Approval]]'', two Grunts, along with Tabitha, tried to steal a curious stone linked with {{p|Groudon}} from the [[Oceanic Museum]]. They successfully escaped with most of the stone. They appeared again in ''[[AG054|Fight for the Meteorite!]]'', where they stole a [[meteorite]] from [[Professor Cozmo]] and used it to power a machine to disturb [[Mt. Chimney]]. They battled [[Team Aqua]] and won, but their plans were ruined by {{Ash}} and {{ashfr}}. Their last appearances were in ''[[AG097|Gaining Groudon!]]'' and ''[[AG098|The Scuffle of Legends!]]'', where the awakening of {{DL|Kyogre and Groudon (Ruby and Sapphire series)|Groudon}} and {{DL|Kyogre and Groudon (Ruby and Sapphire series)|Kyogre}} caused mass destruction before the two Pokémon calmed down. No Team Magma Grunts were seen again after this episode, with the exception of [[Brodie]], who appeared as an independent criminal in ''[[AG119|The Ribbon Cup Caper]]''.

